Lab 1
Questions 1. What is a class?
A Java class is a blueprint or template that defines the fields (data) and methods (behavior) shared by all objects created from it.

 2. What is an object?
 An object is an instance of a class

 3. Can two objects from the same class have different values?
 Yes

